The OWASP Tesing Project has been in development for many years. 

The aim of the project is to help people understand the the what, why, where, and how of testing web applications. 

  The OWASP Testing Guide provides flexible security-testing guidance and promotes integrating 
  throughout the software development life cycle instead of relying only on penetration testing. 

  The OWASP testing framework, validated by industry experts(while not everyone has agreed) helps 
  organizations build secure software while impriving security culture through practical guidance, 
  education, consensus, and experience.

  The rest of this guide is organized as follows: 
  The introduction covers the pre-requisites of testing web applications and the scope of testing. 
  The OWASP Testing Framework and explanation of its techniques and tasks in relation to the 
  various phases of software development life cycle. 
  This is followed by how to test for specific vulnerabilities. 

